 17592186045417] [17592186524844 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186524827 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524844 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524844 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524844 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186524827 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524844 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "079db36a-f121-5453-be8e-d40d62051237" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524950 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186524476 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524950 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186524480 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524950 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186524512 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524950 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186524645 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524950 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186524764 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524950 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524950 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524950 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186524480 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524950 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fc3a16ca-ab9d-5910-8403-1994cf7ec17a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524954 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186524416 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524954 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186524432 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524954 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186524443 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524954 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186524464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524954 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186524685 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524954 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524954 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524954 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186524416 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524954 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "feddc0fa-b88d-5ca9-bd43-99d017ae0768" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524999 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186524844 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524999 #edb/ref 1069 "q-94800" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524999 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524999 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${a}_{11}=-7$ and $det(A)=-3$\n\nII. ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is negative-definite\n\nIII. $A$ is positive-definite" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524999 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7aa930b4-3c77-5008-aaf5-9bbf298703c7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524999 #edb/ref 1074 "Let ${Δ}_{i}$ for $i=1,2,…,n$  denote the leading principal minors of an $n\\times n$ matrix $A.$ Then, according to Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is \n\n- positive-definite if and only if ${Δ}_{i}>0$ for all $i=1,2,…,n,$\n\n- negative-definite if and only if, for all $i=1,2,…,n,$ we have ${Δ}_{i}<0$ when $i$ is odd, and ${Δ}_{i}>0$ when $i$ is even.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, ${a}_{11}=-7$ and \n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}-7 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|=3.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true, while statement III is false. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Δ}_{1} & ={a}_{11}=-7<0, \\\\ {Δ}_{2} & =|\\begin{aligned}-7 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|=3>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by Sylvester's criterion, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x,$ and the matrix $A,$ are negative-definite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525014 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186524950 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525014 #edb/ref 1069 "q-94796" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525014 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525014 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}].$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The eigenvalues of $A$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=4$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=6$\n\nII. ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ is negative-definite\n\nIII. $A$ is positive-definite" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525014 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "95072baf-8f6f-5ac9-b278-bac347e84d65" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525014 #edb/ref 1074 "Given a quadratic form $Q(x)={x}^{T}Ax,$ we have the following theorem:\n\n- $Q$ is positive-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are positive,\n\n- $Q$ is positive semi-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are non-negative (note that positive semi-definite quadratic forms include all positive-definite quadratic forms),\n\n- $Q$ is negative-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are negative,\n\n- $Q$ is negative semi-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are non-positive (note that negative semi-definite quadratic forms include all negative-definite quadratic forms), and\n\n- $Q$ is indefinite if and only if $A$ has both positive and negative eigenvalues.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Computing the characteristic equation of $A,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-5-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 1 & -5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-5-\\lambda )(-5-\\lambda )-1 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+10\\lambda +24 & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =-6,\\,-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true, while statement III is false. Since all the eigenvalues of $A$ are negative, the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,A\\,x$ (as well as the matrix $A$) is negative-definite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525025 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186524954 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525025 #edb/ref 1069 "q-94788" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525025 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525025 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following quadratic forms over ${R}^{3}$ are negative-definite?\n\nI. ${x}^{T}\\,Qx,$ where the eigenvalues of $Q$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\lambda }_{2}=-3$ and ${\\lambda }_{3}=-9$\n\nII. ${x}^{T}\\,Rx,$ where the eigenvalues of $R$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=0,$ ${\\lambda }_{2}=5$ and ${\\lambda }_{3}=-5$\n\nIII. ${x}^{T}\\,Sx,$ where the eigenvalues of $S$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-6,$ ${\\lambda }_{2}=10$ and ${\\lambda }_{3}=-3$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525025 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "aa5d7a51-2b25-530e-bc34-f2b29d7db7d9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525025 #edb/ref 1074 "Given a quadratic form $Q(x)={x}^{T}Ax,$ we have the following theorem:\n\n- $Q$ is positive-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are positive,\n\n- $Q$ is positive semi-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are non-negative (note that positive semi-definite quadratic forms include all positive-definite quadratic forms),\n\n- $Q$ is negative-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are negative,\n\n- $Q$ is negative semi-definite if and only if all the eigenvalues of $A$ are non-positive (note that negative semi-definite quadratic forms include all negative-definite quadratic forms), and\n\n- $Q$ is indefinite if and only if $A$ has both positive and negative eigenvalues.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our quadratic forms in turn. \n\n- Quadratic form I is negative-definite. Indeed, all of the eigenvalues of $Q$ are negative.\n\n- Quadratic form II is *not* negative-definite since not all of the eigenvalues of $R$ are negative (for example, ${\\lambda }_{2}=5$ is not negative).\n\n- Quadratic form III is *not* negative-definite since not all of the eigenvalues of $S$ are negative (${\\lambda }_{2}=10$ is not negative).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525067 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "014ca587-44a7-5c4b-a2b6-7b58d26e96d2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525067 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186524999 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525071 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186525097 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525071 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "06a5f906-8b72-514b-9062-d1bf33299610" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525071 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186525025 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525094 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186525071 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525094 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "561ae071-c31b-5dd5-8e25-204838ce97f8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525094 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186162638 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525097 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186525067 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525097 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5937adbb-f9b5-52b1-9c19-002f11b099e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525097 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186525014 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525118 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186525094 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525118 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a02e4cde-95d3-5443-90f2-5b20307605ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525118 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186162636 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
